Hi Marcelo,

irace waits for jobs in slurm using "squeue -j jobid --noheader". See the function slurm.job.finished() in R/cluster.R

Your target-runner has to print the jobid in stdout, otherwise irace cannot use it later to detect when a job has finished. Also, if the job is still running, squeue must return exit code zero and print the jobid in its stdout. Otherwise, irace will believe that the job is done. Perhaps your squeue command behaves differently?

Cheers,

Manuel.

